/** \file p4_config.dox
 * \brief Configuration dictionary for p4Reduce.
 * \author Jared R. Males
 */

/** \addtogroup p4reduce_user_guide
 * @{
 *
 * \page p4_configuration_dictionary p4Reduce configuration dictionary
 *
 * This dictionary adds P4 settings to the shared \ref common_configuration_dictionary
 * "common configuration dictionary". Long options use `--dotted.key value`; configuration files require a bare key
 * under `[section]`, as described in the shared dictionary. The key/value columns use dotted shorthand only to keep
 * the tables compact. The FITS-keyword column names the card written to final and saved
 * PSF-subtracted products. Keys containing spaces are emitted automatically as `HIERARCH` cards.
 * Analytic-PSF settings are intentionally absent from the ordinary science header; their provenance is recorded only
 * in the opt-in PSF products described below.
 *
 * \section p4_app_dictionary Application mode and scope
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | FITS keyword | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--mode` | `mode=basic` | — | `basic` or `normal` | `basic` | Exact aliases for one configured, target-only P4 reduction. |
 * | `--showTiming` | `showTiming=true` | — | bool | `false` | Print the completed P4 reduction timing report to standard output. |
 *
 * `p4Reduce` currently rejects RDI configuration and does not provide saved-product `postprocess`. Its external grid
 * scheduling is deliberately not an application mode: run separate fully specified configurations instead.
 *
 * \section p4_geometry_dictionary Search annuli and output support
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | FITS keyword | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--geom.minRadius` | `geom.minRadius=3.5,6,8` | `HIERARCH P4 MIN RADIUS` | strictly ordered real pixels | required | Inclusive inner radii of P4 search annuli. |
 * | `--geom.maxRadius` | `geom.maxRadius=6,8,10` | `HIERARCH P4 MAX RADIUS` | matching ordered real-pixel vector | required | Exclusive outer radii. Annuli may not overlap. |
 *
 * Both geometry vectors and every P4 model setting may be omitted when `preProcess.only=true`; that mode stops after
 * shared preprocessing and never constructs P4 regions.
 *
 * Detector mode rejects geometry whose mapped predictor interpolation footprint crosses an image edge. Rotated mode
 * instead tests the direct detector-frame target and predictor footprints over every input frame and invalidates a
 * local sky-pixel fit when any required footprint is incomplete. To retain science over `[r0,r1)`, calculate halo
 * annuli beyond both boundaries, then interpret/crop the desired science interval after finalization. Merely widening
 * the first science annulus changes its predictor geometry; a separate support annulus preserves the core model.
 *
 * \section p4_model_dictionary Predictor region and PCA modes
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | FITS keyword | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--p4.regressionFrame` | `p4.regressionFrame=rotated` | `HIERARCH P4 FRAME` | `detector` or `rotated` | `detector` | Coordinate frame of the local regression. `detector` preserves the original uncentered algorithm; `rotated` uses direct sky-aligned sampling, a centered fit, and uncentered predictor application. |
 * | `--p4.numberImages` | `p4.numberImages=1` | `HIERARCH P4 NUMBER IMAGES` | nonnegative integer | `0` | For detector-frame regression, append `N` nearest qualifying earlier and `N` nearest qualifying later physical-PSF-disk blocks to each predictor row. At endpoints, extra qualifying images from the available side replace missing blocks. Each side must rotate by at least `2 * p4.psfRadius` at the annulus mean radius. P4 lowers an unattainable request to the greatest positive structurally usable radius, or uses same-image predictors when none exists. Values greater than zero are invalid with `regressionFrame=rotated`. |
 * | `--p4.localStampSize` | `p4.localStampSize=11` | `HIERARCH P4 LOCAL STAMP SIZE` | zero or positive odd integer | `0` | Opt into one finite-amplitude pixel-local refit and return this square sky-stamp width. Zero preserves the complete reduction. See \ref p4_local_dictionary. |
 * | `--p4.modeFractions` | `p4.modeFractions=0.01,0.03,...` | `HIERARCH P4 MODE FRACTIONS` | finite, strictly increasing values in `(0,1]` | required | Requested PCA fractions. Each becomes `floor(fraction * min(T,K))` in detector mode or `floor(fraction * min(T-1,K))` in rotated mode; zero or duplicate realized counts are rejected. |
 * | `--p4.orDeltaRadiusInner` | `p4.orDeltaRadiusInner=pixels` | `HIERARCH P4 OR DELTA RADIUS INNER` | positive real pixels | required | Inward radial extent of the local annular predictor wedge. |
 * | `--p4.orDeltaRadiusOuter` | `p4.orDeltaRadiusOuter=pixels` | `HIERARCH P4 OR DELTA RADIUS OUTER` | positive real pixels | required | Outward radial extent of that wedge. |
 * | `--p4.orArcHalfWidth` | `p4.orArcHalfWidth=pixels` | `HIERARCH P4 OR ARC HALF WIDTH` | nonnegative real arc length | required | Azimuthal half-width of the predictor wedge, expressed as arc length at the region radius; `0` uses only `orMaxHalfAngle`. |
 * | `--p4.orMaxHalfAngle` | `p4.orMaxHalfAngle=degrees` | `HIERARCH P4 OR MAX HALF ANGLE` | real degrees in `(0,180]` | required | Cap on the predictor wedge's angular half-width; `180` permits the full 360-degree annulus. |
 * | `--p4.rankTolerance` | `p4.rankTolerance=1e-12` | `HIERARCH P4 RANK TOLERANCE` | real in `[0,1)` | `1e-12` | Relative rank criterion: a mode is retained only when `lambda > tolerance * lambdaMax`. `0` accepts all positive returned eigenvalues, including roundoff-positive nulls. |
 *
 * For a positive `p4.numberImages`, `T` is the number of retained central targets in that annulus after temporal
 * neighbor selection, and `K` is the original OR predictor count plus `2 * p4.numberImages` physical-PSF-disk blocks.
 *
 * Detector mode regresses one fixed detector-pixel time series on its local OR without implicit centering or an
 * intercept. Rotated mode constructs one fixed sky-frame OR, maps its target and predictor coordinates directly back
 * through each frame's inverse derotation, and applies one cubic interpolation in the preprocessed detector image.
 * It does not materialize a rotated cube or interpolate fractional OR coordinates twice.
 *
 * Rotated mode centers the target and every predictor over the same complete `T`-frame set when estimating the
 * coefficients. It then applies those coefficients to the original uncentered, post-preprocessing predictor values
 * and subtracts that prediction from the original sampled target. Centering imposes the structural `T-1` limit even
 * when `p4.rankTolerance=0`; at least two frames are required. A constant target offset does not affect the fit and
 * passes through to the residual, while predictor DC levels affect the applied prediction and residual mean.
 *
 * \warning `rotated` is an experimental numerical-reference mode and has failed its current AF Lep/NACO scientific
 * acceptance comparison. Its products were effectively the target-only sky stacks because the centered objective
 * did not constrain the combined residual baseline. No replacement baseline rule is implemented. Retain the
 * default `detector` setting for science reductions.
 *
 * P4 automatically uses the smaller temporal or predictor Gram formulation, performs the normal-equation work in
 * double precision, and applies the same truncated rank policy in both regression frames. The Gram choice is not a
 * configurable backend.
 *
 * \section p4_memory_dictionary Memory and worker management
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | FITS keyword | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--p4.memoryFraction` | `p4.memoryFraction=0.8` | `HIERARCH P4 MEMORY FRACTION` | real in `[0,1]` | `0.8` | Fraction of Linux `MemAvailable` usable by future P4 allocations. P4 reduces each annulus's worker count when its compact retained storage plus estimated private workspaces would exceed this budget. `0` disables automatic discovery and limiting. |
 *
 * With a configured final combination and `output.outputPSFSub=false`, residuals are retained only for owned search
 * pixels. One full science/validity cube pair is materialized for each output mode, finalized, and released before the
 * next pair is allocated. `combine.method=none` and `output.outputPSFSub=true` retain the full residual and validity
 * cubes because those products are explicitly requested. P4 records the available-memory snapshot, selected budget,
 * compact-storage and materialization estimates, per-annulus worker estimate, maximum worker count, and effective
 * worker count in `HIERARCH P4 ...` FITS cards. `OMP_NUM_THREADS` remains a valid upper limit and is never increased.
 *
 * \section p4_local_dictionary Finite-amplitude pixel-local refitting
 *
 * A positive `p4.localStampSize` replaces the complete output-field calculation with one exact local trial. The
 * trial uses the existing `fake.fileName`, `fake.sep`, `fake.PA`, `fake.contrast`, and optional
 * `fake.scaleFileName` settings. Exactly one separation, PA, and finite contrast must be supplied, and
 * `fake.method=single` is required. Unlike frozen-model PSF calculation, the trial perturbation is added to the
 * target and every same-image or positive-`numberImages` predictor sample before the ordinary P4 eigensolve. Each
 * detector regression used by the local sky stamp is therefore refit at the configured finite amplitude.
 *
 * The initial exact contract requires `preProcess.skip=true`, `p4.regressionFrame=detector`, enabled derotation, a
 * final `combine.method`, `adi.postMedSub=false`, and `output.outputPSFSub=false`. Frozen-model settings
 * `p4.psfFile`, `p4.outputPSFModels`, and `p4.psfFilter` cannot be combined with this path. The fake template must
 * represent the already-preprocessed P4 input stage; inherited fake injection is inactive when preprocessing is
 * skipped, so the input cube remains pristine and trial flux does not accumulate across calls.
 *
 * Image and template centers use the geometric convention `0.5*(N-1)`. For a final-sky separation `r` and PA
 * `theta`, the continuous source coordinate is
 *
 * \f[
 *   x_s = \tfrac{1}{2}(N_x-1)-r\sin\theta, \qquad
 *   y_s = \tfrac{1}{2}(N_y-1)+r\cos\theta.
 * \f]
 *
 * The odd output lattice is anchored at `floor(source+0.5)` in each axis, but the source itself remains at the
 * continuous coordinate recorded by `HIERARCH P4 LOCAL SOURCE ROW/COLUMN`. The template is never recentered onto
 * that integer anchor. Its internal centered crop is the smallest dimension at least `localStampSize` having the
 * same parity as the detector and source template. Thus an 11-pixel result on an even-sized detector uses a centered
 * 12-pixel template crop and retains the original half-pixel center. Detector and source-template parity must match,
 * as in ordinary fake injection.
 *
 * Only detector residuals touched by the exact cubic derotation footprints are retained. The standard final-image
 * product becomes a `localStampSize x localStampSize x modeCount` cube with
 * `HIERARCH P4 PRODUCT ROLE=LOCAL_RESIDUAL`. A second zero/one cube uses the same mode order and is named by inserting
 * `local_validity` before the normal four-digit sequence, for example
 * `finim_local_validity_0000.fits`; exact filenames instead become `<stem>_local_validity<extension>`. Both products
 * carry the integer full-image origin, continuous source coordinate, center/lattice conventions, actual template
 * crop dimensions, unique detector-fit count, sparse residual-sample count, fake-source provenance, and the
 * `POST_PREPROCESS_P4_INPUT` injection stage. The memory policy includes the retained sparse dependency map and
 * records its exact dynamic allocation as `HIERARCH P4 LOCAL GEOMETRY BYTES`.
 *
 * For example, evaluate one 11-pixel negative trial against an already-preprocessed input configuration:
 *
 * \code{.sh}
 * p4Reduce -c prepared-p4.conf \
 *   --preProcess.skip=true \
 *   --p4.localStampSize=11 \
 *   --fake.method=single \
 *   --fake.fileName=/path/post-preprocess-psf.fits \
 *   --fake.sep=13 --fake.PA=100 --fake.contrast=-0.001
 * \endcode
 *
 * \section p4_optimizer_dictionary Negative-companion optimization
 *
 * The optional `[p4Optimize]` layer repeatedly calls the exact finite-amplitude local path against one pristine,
 * already-loaded target cube. With `fitPosition=false`, separation and PA remain fixed at the single configured
 * `[fake]` tuple while a deterministic bounded Brent search minimizes contrast. With `fitPosition=true`, that
 * contrast result seeds a bounded Nelder-Mead search in Cartesian row offset, column offset, and contrast. A second
 * fixed-position dense+Brent contrast fit validates the final photometry. The Cartesian convention is the exact
 * inverse of P4 local processing and therefore preserves the `0.5*(N-1)` image center and avoids PA wrap internally.
 * All modes use the selected output plane's uniform mean-square residual inside an aperture centered on the continuous
 * source coordinate.
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | Best-product FITS keyword | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--p4Optimize.enabled` | `p4Optimize.enabled=true` | `HIERARCH P4 OPTIMIZER` | bool | `false` | Run negative-companion optimization instead of one ordinary reduction. Requires the pixel-local contract above. |
 * | `--p4Optimize.modeFraction` | `p4Optimize.modeFraction=0.15` | `HIERARCH P4 OPT MODE FRACTION` | exact member of `p4.modeFractions` | `0.15` | Single output plane used by the scalar merit. A nearest plane is never selected silently. |
 * | `--p4Optimize.apertureRadius` | `p4Optimize.apertureRadius=5` | `HIERARCH P4 OPT APERTURE RADIUS` | nonnegative real pixels | `0` | Uniform-L2 aperture radius. Zero selects `2*p4.psfRadius`; the complete aperture must fit inside the local stamp and every included pixel must be valid. |
 * | `--p4Optimize.fitPosition` | `p4Optimize.fitPosition=true` | `HIERARCH P4 OPT FIT POSITION` | bool | `false` | Jointly fit Cartesian astrometry and contrast. False preserves the fixed-position contrast-only path. |
 * | `--p4Optimize.contrastLower` | `p4Optimize.contrastLower=-0.05` | `HIERARCH P4 OPT CONTRAST LOWER` | finite real | `-0.05` | Inclusive signed lower contrast bound. |
 * | `--p4Optimize.contrastUpper` | `p4Optimize.contrastUpper=0` | `HIERARCH P4 OPT CONTRAST UPPER` | finite real, greater than lower and at most zero | `0` | Inclusive signed upper contrast bound. The configured initial `fake.contrast` must lie inside both bounds. |
 * | `--p4Optimize.maxEvaluations` | `p4Optimize.maxEvaluations=192` | `HIERARCH P4 OPT EVALUATIONS` | integer at least `validationSamples+3`; joint minimum `2*(validationSamples+16)+4` | `64` | Hard limit on distinct local P4 calls. Joint mode reserves two complete contrast stages; 192 is recommended for a 21-point full fit. |
 * | `--p4Optimize.validationSamples` | `p4Optimize.validationSamples=21` | — | integer at least 3 | `21` | Uniform dense-grid size, including both bounds. |
 * | `--p4Optimize.parameterTolerance` | `p4Optimize.parameterTolerance=1e-5` | — | positive finite real | `1e-5` | Absolute contrast-width tolerance and, in joint mode, Cartesian simplex diameter tolerance in pixels. |
 * | `--p4Optimize.meritTolerance` | `p4Optimize.meritTolerance=1e-6` | — | nonnegative finite real | `1e-6` | Combined absolute/relative merit allowance, scaled by `max(1,abs(merit))`, for simplex convergence and dense-basin agreement. |
 * | `--p4Optimize.positionBound` | `p4Optimize.positionBound=1` | `HIERARCH P4 OPT POSITION BOUND` | positive finite real pixels in joint mode | `1` | Symmetric row/column bound around the initial configured source. Each Cartesian coordinate is bounded independently. |
 * | `--p4Optimize.uncertaintyBlocks` | `p4Optimize.uncertaintyBlocks=8` | — | integer at least 2 | `8` | Reserved contiguous jackknife block count for the later uncertainty stage. |
 * | `--p4Optimize.outputPrefix` | `p4Optimize.outputPrefix=p4Negative_` | — | nonempty relative prefix | `p4Negative_` | Product prefix inside `output.directory`; parent directories are created automatically. |
 *
 * Intermediate trials disable both ordinary final-image output and P4 diagnostics. At completion the common output
 * directory receives `<prefix>merit.csv`, `<prefix>summary.yaml`, `<prefix>best.fits`, and
 * `<prefix>best_validity.fits`. The two FITS cubes own only the best local result and contain ordinary HCI/P4 cards,
 * the selected mode, aperture, bounds, fitted separation/PA/contrast, Cartesian displacement, evaluation count,
 * position and contrast convergence, dense agreement, and product role. A converged result also writes
 * `<prefix>best.conf`, containing the fitted `[fake]` tuple. An exhausted or dense-disagreeing search still records
 * its best finite evaluation and explicit failure status, but does not write the configuration fragment and returns
 * failure from `p4Reduce`. The joint merit CSV identifies `seed-dense`, `seed-brent`, `simplex`, `final-dense`, and
 * `final-brent` evaluations and records both polar and Cartesian trial coordinates.
 *
 * For the AF Lep 11-pixel local setup, add:
 *
 * \code{.ini}
 * [p4Optimize]
 * enabled=true
 * modeFraction=0.15
 * apertureRadius=5
 * contrastLower=-0.05
 * contrastUpper=0
 * maxEvaluations=64
 * validationSamples=21
 * parameterTolerance=1e-5
 * meritTolerance=1e-6
 * outputPrefix=p4Negative_
 * \endcode
 *
 * The existing `fake.sep` and `fake.PA` remain the fixed location. Set the existing `fake.contrast` to any finite
 * initial value inside `[-0.05,0]`; it is recorded for provenance but the required dense scan supplies the numerical
 * starting basin.
 *
 * To fit astrometry as well, retain the same initial `[fake]` tuple and change the optimizer controls to:
 *
 * \code{.ini}
 * [p4Optimize]
 * enabled=true
 * fitPosition=true
 * positionBound=1
 * modeFraction=0.15
 * apertureRadius=5
 * contrastLower=-0.05
 * contrastUpper=0
 * maxEvaluations=192
 * validationSamples=21
 * parameterTolerance=1e-5
 * meritTolerance=1e-6
 * outputPrefix=p4Negative_
 * \endcode
 *
 * \section p4_psf_dictionary Frozen-model PSF calculation and output
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | PSF-product FITS keyword | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--p4.psfFile` | `p4.psfFile=/path/template.fits` | `HIERARCH P4 PSF TEMPLATE` | readable, finite two-dimensional FITS image | unset | Centered PSF template at the same post-preprocessing stage as the P4 input. Setting the path enables local frozen-model response calculation without changing the science products. The stored normalization is preserved. |
 * | `--p4.psfStampSize` | `p4.psfStampSize=11` | `HIERARCH P4 PSF STAMP SIZE` | positive integer | `0` | Row and column size of each final square response stamp. Both odd and even sizes use geometric centers. Required when `psfFile` is set. |
 * | `--p4.outputPSFModels` | `p4.outputPSFModels=true` | — | bool | `false` | Reconstruct, combine, and write one compact final-frame response field per P4 mode. Requires `psfFile` and a final `combine.method`. |
 * | `--p4.psfFilter` | `p4.psfFilter=true` | `HIERARCH P4 PSF FILTER` (PSF products) | bool | `false` | Apply the signed, normalized spatially variable PSF filter and write separate full-image products. Requires `psfFile`, an odd `psfStampSize`, and a final `combine.method`; it does not require `outputPSFModels=true`. |
 * | `--p4.psfFilterMinGoodFract` | `p4.psfFilterMinGoodFract=0.8` | `HIERARCH P4 PSF FILTER MIN GOOD FRACTION` (PSF products) | real in `[0,1]` | `1` | Minimum fraction of the full stamp area having valid PSF samples and finite in-bounds science samples. Values below the threshold have explicit zero filter validity and NaN filtered amplitude. |
 * | `--p4.psfOutputPrefix` | `p4.psfOutputPrefix=p4PSF_` | — | nonempty path prefix | `p4PSF_` | Compact model/manifest prefix inside `output.directory`; parent directories are created automatically. Filter cubes instead follow the ordinary final-image name and sequence. |
 *
 * For example, enable PSF reconstruction in a configuration file with literal sectioned syntax:
 *
 * \code{.ini}
 * [p4]
 * psfFile=/path/template.fits
 * psfStampSize=11
 * outputPSFModels=true
 * psfFilter=true
 * psfFilterMinGoodFract=0.8
 * \endcode
 *
 * The initial implementation accepts `p4.psfFile` only with `p4.regressionFrame=detector`,
 * `p4.numberImages=0`, and `adi.postMedSub=false`. Unsupported combinations are rejected before regression. The
 * template is sampled with zero exterior padding, but the retained local response is enlarged as needed to preserve
 * odd/even sampling phase and support arbitrary derotation angles. Local and reconstruction storage is included in
 * the P4 memory-policy checks. Final reconstruction workers are reduced when their bounded frame-stamp scratch would
 * exceed the configured budget.
 *
 * With `outputPSFModels=true`, the common output directory receives:
 *
 * - `<prefix>coordinates.fits`, an `S x 4` image whose columns are `row,column,region,regionSearch`;
 * - `<prefix>model_NNNN.fits`, a `psfStampSize x psfStampSize x S` cube for each zero-based mode index;
 * - `<prefix>validity_NNNN.fits`, an `S x 1` exact zero/one source-center validity image for each mode; and
 * - `<prefix>manifest.fits`, a one-element completion product.
 *
 * With `psfFilter=true`, it additionally receives four full-frame cubes in the ordinary P4 mode order. Their names
 * follow the resolved ordinary final-image name and share its sequence number. For the default `finim_` prefix these
 * are:
 *
 * - `finim_filtered_NNNN.fits`, containing `sum(H*I)/sum(H*H)` where the local fit is valid;
 * - `finim_filter_normalization_NNNN.fits`, containing the retained `sum(H*H)` denominator;
 * - `finim_filter_support_NNNN.fits`, containing the usable-sample count divided by the full stamp area; and
 * - `finim_filter_validity_NNNN.fits`, containing exact zero/one filter validity.
 *
 * Filtering is independent of model persistence: `psfFilter=true, outputPSFModels=false` writes the four filtered
 * products and manifest without writing coordinate, model, or model-validity products. The ordinary final image is
 * never replaced. Each filtered product mirrors the complete ordinary final-image FITS header and adds its P4 PSF
 * role, filter, and source-path provenance. With `output.exactFName=true`, the role is inserted before the configured
 * filename extension instead of a sequence number. An odd filter stamp is required because its geometric center then
 * maps exactly to the integer output coordinate; even response stamps remain valid when only `outputPSFModels` is
 * enabled.
 *
 * Plane `s` in every model cube belongs to row `s` of the coordinate image. Individual unsupported stamp samples are
 * NaN in the model cube even when the source center is valid. Every file is published by a temporary-file rename.
 * The manifest is first published with `HIERARCH P4 PSF COMPLETE = 0` and is replaced with value `1` only after the
 * complete configured product set has been written. Consumers must require value `1`, use the manifest's mode count,
 * and ignore stale extra files left by an earlier run with more modes.
 *
 * \section p4_exclusion_dictionary Signal exclusion
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | FITS keyword | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--p4.psfRadius` | `p4.psfRadius=pixels` | `HIERARCH P4 PSF RADIUS` | positive real pixels | required | Physical central radius excluded from predictors. |
 * | `--p4.exclusionRadiusBuffer` | `p4.exclusionRadiusBuffer=0.5` | `HIERARCH P4 EXCLUSION RADIUS BUFFER` | nonnegative real pixels | required | Explicit additional radius applied to the physical exclusion. `0.5` reproduces the prototype's effective buffer. |
 * | `--p4.exclusionPolicy` | `p4.exclusionPolicy=sampleCenter` | `HIERARCH P4 EXCLUSION POLICY` | `sampleCenter` or `kernelSupport` | required | Defines how the buffered exclusion is tested. |
 *
 * `sampleCenter` rejects a predictor sample when its interpolated sample center lies inside the buffered disk. It is the
 * closest match to the prototype's center-only mask. `kernelSupport` rejects a predictor column when any pixel in its
 * nominal cubic-interpolation support lies inside the disk. In rotated mode that test uses the exact one-stage
 * detector-frame footprint over every search pixel and input frame before fixing the annulus-wide predictor count.
 * Thus `kernelSupport` is more conservative near the boundary, but it is not simply a larger `psfRadius`: the exact
 * rejection depends on fractional location and the orientation of the four-by-four detector footprint.
 *
 * \section p4_validity_dictionary Masks, rank, and invalid local fits
 *
 * Common input masks are authoritative. In detector mode a local fit becomes invalid when its target or predictor
 * support touches a masked pixel. In rotated mode the target and every predictor must have complete nominal cubic
 * support in every frame, and every pixel in those detector-frame footprints must be nonzero in the common mask.
 * Failure in one frame invalidates the sky search pixel in every frame and output plane; P4 never drops a different
 * frame set for different predictor columns.
 *
 * Numerical-rank failure invalidates only the unsupported output planes. P4 carries all invalidity in a separate
 * validity cube through the applicable final-processing operations; invalid values become NaN only after final
 * arithmetic. Nonfinite target input remains a hard reduction error.
 *
 * \section p4_rotated_preprocessing_dictionary Optional baseline preprocessing
 *
 * Rotated regression estimates coefficients from temporal fluctuations but applies them to complete predictor values,
 * so its residual baseline is defined by the raw predictor levels after inherited preprocessing. The inherited
 * `preProcess.subradprof=true` option can first subtract a median radial profile from each detector image. The inherited
 * `preProcess.meanSubMethod=medianImage` option can instead, or subsequently, subtract a temporal median detector-frame
 * PSF. These operations precede the rotated regression's internal centering and alter the input from which both target
 * and predictors are sampled.
 *
 * Neither baseline operation is required. Radial-profile subtraction can bias localized sources, and median-image
 * subtraction can self-subtract companions when field rotation or temporal sampling is inadequate. Use injected-source
 * tests to measure throughput for the chosen preprocessing, and use `preProcess.skip=true` only for input whose prior
 * preprocessing is understood.
 *
 * These detector-frame operations do not remove the residual-mean ambiguity in the centered rotated objective.
 * Temporal mean subtraction and frame-dependent rotation do not commute, so a detector-pixel zero mean does not
 * imply a fixed-sky zero mean. A future rotated science mode requires an independently justified stellar-baseline
 * model or prior.
 *
 * \section p4_rotated_final_dictionary ADI and combination interaction
 *
 * `adi.postMedSub=true` is invalid with `p4.regressionFrame=rotated`: subtracting the temporal median at a fixed sky
 * pixel would impose a second sky-fixed baseline policy after the predictor subtraction and confound its throughput
 * contract. Rotated residual and validity cubes are already in the final sky frame, so the shared final lifecycle
 * skips derotation and proceeds to validity-aware combination and output. `combine.noDerotate` applies only to
 * detector-frame residuals and has no effect in rotated mode; users do not need to set it to prevent double
 * derotation.
 *
 * \section p4_diagnostics_dictionary Diagnostics and progress
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | FITS keyword | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--p4.writeDiagnostics` | `p4.writeDiagnostics=true` | `HIERARCH P4 WRITE DIAGNOSTICS` | bool | `false` | Writes ownership, validity, canonical-region, rank, timing, and summary FITS diagnostics. Every diagnostic carries `HIERARCH P4 FRAME` provenance. |
 * | `--p4.diagnosticDirectory` | `p4.diagnosticDirectory=/path` | — | writable directory; required when diagnostics are enabled | `.` | Destination for P4 diagnostic products; missing parent directories are created automatically. |
 *
 * Geometry construction reports each annulus's search-pixel and retained predictor count. A memory line then reports
 * its estimated private MiB per worker and effective/pre-limit worker counts. Regression status reports the active
 * annulus, completed/total local fits, rate, local ETA, and cumulative overall progress to
 * standard error. `p4Validity_*.fits` is in detector coordinates for detector regression and in sky coordinates for
 * rotated regression. Final and PSF-subtracted FITS products record the selection as the long keyword
 * `HIERARCH P4 FRAME = 'detector'` or `HIERARCH P4 FRAME = 'rotated'`. Temporal centering for coefficient fitting and
 * application to the uncentered predictors are intrinsic to the documented `rotated` definition.
 * `p4Timing.fits` schema 3 has one row, in seconds: geometry elapsed, regression elapsed, total sampling, same-image
 * target/OR sampling, additional-image PSF-disk sampling, Gram-construction, eigensolve/rank-selection, and
 * projection/residual aggregate OpenMP-worker time. Schema 4 appends aggregate local-PSF worker time when
 * `p4.psfFile` is set. Schema 5 appends elapsed final-field reconstruction/product time when either
 * `p4.outputPSFModels=true` or `p4.psfFilter=true`.
 * Worker totals can exceed elapsed time when local fits run concurrently; `HIERARCH P4 TIMING SCHEMA` and
 * `HIERARCH P4 TIMING COLUMNS` define the persisted layout.
 *
 * @}
 */
